## Scope

`git diff --stat 4eebabbb2..65b8325b0` lists 16 files. The production code files are
frame.tsx, done-mark.tsx, look.css, highlight.ts, and read-along-passage.tsx. The other
files are tests, the Phase 2b browser gate script, plan.md, spec.md, and gate logs.
The security surface is small: no route, handler, schema, migration, cookie, header,
or dependency change enters the range. Security applicability: applicable.

## Named security deltas

1. frame.tsx (apps/storytime/app/[locale]/frame.tsx). The inline style now holds one
   value only: `{ "--title-chars": title.length }`. The earlier `clamp()` template is
   gone. The value is a number, so no week text can reach the style attribute. The
   title is a React text child, so React escapes it. Result: pass.
2. read-along (packages/read-along/lib/highlight.ts and read-along-passage.tsx). The
   changes set HIGHLIGHT_CLASSES.currentWord arbitrary Tailwind color values and two
   focus-visible class strings. The changes touch class strings only. No handler,
   state, or data-flow change. Result: pass.
3. look.css. The grep for `@import` returns no match. The grep for `http` returns no
   match. Every `url()` value is a relative `look/places/*.webp` path, and one
   background holds a pre-existing `data:image/svg+xml` value. No `@font-face` and no
   font fetch enter the range. Result: pass.
4. The gate script (apps/storytime/__tests__/look-phase2-browser-gate.sh). Line 74
   makes TMP_DIR with `mktemp -d -t storytime-look-p2-XXXXXX`. FIXTURE is
   `$TMP_DIR/content`. The fixture content is written only under TMP_DIR. Line 2780
   writes accounts.csv into `$TMP_DIR/accounts`. `cleanup` removes TMP_DIR.
   MEDIA_ROOT defaults to `~/Desktop/handoff/w01-storytime-app-package-r2` and stays
   outside the repository. The database is an ephemeral podman Postgres container
   with no volume. `make-accounts.ts` runs against that container. The teacher sign-in
   prints only `teacher_session_cookies=<count>`. Line 2901 sets STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES=1
   and the other STORYTIME_* names in the next start process environment only. A grep
   of apps/storytime returns 37 hits for the three names, and none of them is in
   apps/storytime/Dockerfile or apps/storytime/cloudbuild.yaml. Result: pass.
5. The sign-in and join pages. `git diff --name-only 4eebabbb2..65b8325b0` over
   apps/storytime/app returns no sign-in, join, login, teacher, auth, or not-found
   file. The pages are unchanged since round 1, so the round 1 checks still hold.
   Result: pass.

## Other checks

The added test code holds no fetch, no http request, no `process.env` write, no
`writeFileSync`, no `innerHTML`, no `__html`, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, and no
`eval` of user data. The one `spawnSync` call runs `git diff` with fixed arguments and
a fixed `cwd`.

The new self-test rows use literal control and mutant objects, so no external input can
make a control pass. The helper-existence check runs `eval` on a fixed name list.

A2 (consent-blind publish gate). The gate script sets `w01.approval.loops.status` to
approved in the TMP_DIR fixture copy only. The shipped week file is untouched. No named
school or person is published. The Storytime content model holds no consent artifact,
and no artifact is needed. A2 does not apply.

A6 (registry overstatement). measure/tracks.md holds the storytime_look_20261107 row
with status text only. No security state reads "resolved". A6 does not apply.

## Verdict

Pass. No blocking finding and no nonblocking finding. The round 2 deltas are brand
tones, class strings, and gate self-tests. Nothing in the range reaches a deploy file,
a secret, a network call, or a tenant boundary.

